1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,000
[roars]

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,000
[narrator] Strange beasts

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:06,000
and monsters.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Vast riches.

5
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,000
Hidden treasures.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Evil haunts.

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:17,000
Uncharted frontiers.

8
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
The mysterious unknown.

9
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The people who are captivated
by the magic in those words...

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:28,000
are called...

11
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Hunters!

12
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:37,000
[theme song plays]

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
[gasps]

14
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:02,000
It's so delightful. I love that look.

15
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:07,000
[Gon] But I've got to say, it was actually
pretty exciting back there.

16
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Huh?

17
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,000
[Gon] I was so scared that all I wanted
to do was run away,

18
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,000
but I couldn't.

19
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
'Cause I was excited at the same time!

20
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Isn't that weird?

21
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:23,000
A x SURPRISING x CHALLENGE

22
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,000
[all panting]

23
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Looks like we made it in time.

24
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,000
But where's Leorio?

25
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,000
There he is.

26
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Man, that stings!
How the hell did I get beat up so badly?

27
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,000
[both gasp]

28
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:59,000
[Leorio] My memory's so hazy,
I can't remember.

29
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
We probably shouldn't tell him
what happened.

30
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,000
You're right.

31
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:05,000
[Killua] Gon.

32
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,000
[Gon] Killua!

33
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
I was starting to think
you weren't gonna make it here.

34
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Or that you didn't make it at all.

35
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:14,000
I just followed the trail
of Leorio's cologne.

36
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:17,000
You tracked his scent? That's how?

37
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Man, Gon!
You really are weird, aren't you?

38
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:23,000
[Satotz] Excellent work, everyone!

39
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:27,000
The Second Phase will take place here,
in the Visca Forest Park.

40
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:32,000
So, I shall now take my leave.
I wish you all the very best of luck.

41
00:03:38,000 --> 00:03:40,000
[gates rumbling]

42
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:55,000
[Menchi] Will all the applicants
who passed the First Phase please enter?

43
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:58,000
Welcome, all!

44
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:01,000
I'm Menchi, your examiner
for the Second Phase.

45
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:04,000
And likewise, I'm Buhara.

46
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:11,000
[Buhara's stomach rumbles]

47
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
-[crowd whispering]
-[man] What was that noise?

48
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Sounds to me like you're getting hungry.

49
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:19,000
Not just hungry, I'm famished!

50
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Well, there you have it.
The Second Phase...

51
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
will be cooking!

52
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:29,000
-Wait... we're cooking?
-Huh?

53
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:35,000
What do you mean, we're cooking?
We came here to take the Hunter Exam.

54
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,000
[Menchi] That's right.

55
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:39,000
The Second Phase of the exam
will be preparing a meal

56
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
that'll satisfy our palates.

57
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:43,000
[man] Why do we have to cook?

58
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Don't you know? It's simple really,
because we're Gourmet Hunters!

59
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Huh? [laughs]

60
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
-[crowd laughing]
-[Todo] Talk about a let down!

61
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:57,000
You hear that? They're Gourmet Hunters!

62
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
[laughing continues]

63
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,000
[Menchi sighs]

64
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:04,000
[Satotz]
Gourmet Hunters, Menchi and Buhara.

65
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:08,000
Their selection as examiners
could prove quite problematic.

66
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Only 50 applicants left.
But, depending on the task,

67
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:17,000
it's possible that fewer than ten
will pass the Second Phase.

68
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
[laughing continues]

69
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:24,000
So, you're both Gourmet Hunters.
And what exactly do you want us to make?

70
00:05:27,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Buhara?

71
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
Today's required ingredient will be pork.

72
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
[man] Pork? You mean like pig meat?

73
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
[Buhara] Feel free to use meat from any
species of pig in Visca Forest.

74
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:45,000
As you see, you'll use these cooking
facilities to prep your pork dishes.

75
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:50,000
To pass the exam, you must create a dish
to satisfy our discriminating palates.

76
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:56,000
But we won't be evaluating taste alone.
So take this seriously. Is that clear?

77
00:05:56,000 --> 00:06:00,000
When we've both eaten our fill,
this portion of the exam will be over.

78
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Okay, enough talk.
Let's just get to it, alright?

79
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:07,000
Let the exam's Second Phase...

80
00:06:07,000 --> 00:06:08,000
[gong sounds]

81
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:10,000
...begin!

82
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:13,000
[hurried footsteps]

83
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:22,000
[Menchi] Any species of pig, huh?
You've got a real mean streak, don't you?

84
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
[Buhara] Well, you did say
I got to pick the ingredient.

85
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,000
There's only one species of pig
in Visca Forest,

86
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,000
but you already knew that.

87
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:32,000
Hmm. I hope nobody gets killed!

88
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:35,000
[indistinct chatter]

89
00:06:39,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Hey! Piggy!

90
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:44,000
[Leorio] We gotta catch a pig
and cook it, huh?

91
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Man, this is way easier than
the First Phase

92
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,000
I just hope it's that simple.

93
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:53,000
[Killua whooping]

94
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
[screams]

95
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:58,000
[all grunt]

96
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,000
What the hell do you think you're doing?

97
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,000
-[Gon] I found them.
-Huh?

98
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,000
[Leorio] Pigs!

99
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:10,000
They're all... chewing on bones.

100
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
Don't tell me... they're carnivores?

101
00:07:15,000 --> 00:07:16,000
[pig roars]

102
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
[all screaming]

103
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,000
[man] What the hell's that?

104
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:28,000
[Leorio panting]

105
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:35,000
[all screaming]

106
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:39,000
These pigs are insane!

107
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
[Buhara] The Great Stamp!

108
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:45,000
The most ferocious pig in the whole world.

109
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:49,000
They use their large, sturdy snouts
to send their predators flying.

110
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,000
You've got to move really quick

111
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,000
unless you want to end up the main course
for their dinner.

112
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,000
[roars]

113
00:07:59,000 --> 00:07:59,000
What?

114
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
[gasps]

115
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:08,000
[yells]

116
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
[pig squealing]

117
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Wait a second...

118
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:32,000
[Gon yells]

119
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:41,000
[squeals]

120
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Huh, that's it! Their foreheads
are their weak spots.

121
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:51,000
I see. that makes sense.

122
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:55,000
They developed tough snouts
to protect their delicate foreheads.

123
00:09:05,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Huh? Oh!

124
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:17,000
-[chuckles]
-Look at that! They sure caught a lot.

125
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:29,000
[Satotz] Hmm. This is an exceptional batch
of applicants, indeed.

126
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:34,000
But the hard part is yet to come.

127
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:38,000
[Todo] Now, eat the pig
and send me to the next phase.

128
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:41,000
Okay, time to judge.

129
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Taste testing...

130
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,000
-[Buhara chuckles]
-[bell rings]

131
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:52,000
-[buzzer sounds]
-Huh?

132
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:54,000
The pork's overcooked.

133
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:57,000
It's way too tough.
It totally ruins the flavor.

134
00:09:57,000 --> 00:10:01,000
-Come on! You haven't even tried it!
-I don't have to! It's obvious.

135
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,000
[grunts angrily]

136
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
There, I hope you enjoy it.

137
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,000
[bell rings]

138
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:10,000
[buzzer sounds]

139
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,000
[gasps] But why?

140
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Charred and dry on the outside,
raw on the inside.

141
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Your fire was way too hot.

142
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:19,000
[bell rings]

143
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,000
[buzzer sounds]

144
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,000
[bell rings]

145
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
[buzzer sounds]

146
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,000
[Menchi] Honestly! They're all just
roasting the entire pig,

147
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:30,000
like it's the only thing
they know how to do.

148
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:32,000
None of them have made any effort at all!

149
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,000
[Leorio] Not one applicant has passed yet.

150
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:41,000
And Menchi has yet to take
a single bite of anyone's entry.

151
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:46,000
Seriously? Can't anyone out there make
something that'll satisfy my taste buds.

152
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:50,000
That's it!
The Second Phase is a cooking test,

153
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
but they're judging us
based on originality and observation.

154
00:10:53,000 --> 00:10:55,000
Oh, I see.

155
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,000
[Buhara laughs gleefully]

156
00:10:57,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Tell me how much you love it.

157
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:03,000
Is this supposed to be a kid's meal?

158
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:07,000
Okay, mine is next.

159
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
It's just like the last one!

160
00:11:12,000 --> 00:11:15,000
The next entry's mine, ready to be judged.

161
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:19,000
Well, finally, something that resembles
an actual dish.

162
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:24,000
[Kurapika] The challenge is to utilize
the facilities and ingredients provided

163
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
to highlight the main feature: the pork.

164
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:30,000
In short, the taste is insignificant.

165
00:11:30,000 --> 00:11:32,000
[Menchi] Gross!

166
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:34,000
[gasps]

167
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:38,000
Presentation is important,
but not at the expense of the flavor.

168
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,000
You're basically no better
than Number 403.

169
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:45,000
-[buzzer sounds]
-[sneers] Better luck next time.

170
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:48,000
No better than 403, huh?

171
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:54,000
[chuckles] That was so much food.
I couldn't take another bite.

172
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Yeah, I'm pretty stuffed, myself.

173
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:01,000
So, none of you passed to the next phase.
Exam's over!

174
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:03,000
[crowd gasps]

175
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:07,000
[Satotz] Just as I feared,
she's reverted to her bad habits.

176
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:13,000
[Beans] What should we do now, Chairman?

177
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,000
[Chairman] I suppose I have no choice.

178
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,000
It's time for a little outing.

179
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:26,000
HUNTER GLOSSARY

180
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:30,000
MENCHI

181
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:34,000
-[man 1] Nobody passed?
-[man 2] Seriously?

182
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
[man 3] Does she really mean that?

183
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,000
[man 4] Wait, so the exam's over?

184
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,000
[man 5] You gotta be kidding!

185
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:47,000
This is unacceptable.
Do ya hear me? I will not accept this!

186
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:50,000
[Menchi] Say what you want,
but you still failed.

187
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:54,000
[Todo] Shut the hell up!
You asked for pork and we gave it to you.

188
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,000
We risked our lives--

189
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Your challenge was to prepare a pork dish
that both examiners would find delicious,

190
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:02,000
and none of you even came close
to succeeding.

191
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:05,000
You all did pretty much
the exact same thing.

192
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:08,000
I mean, it's like you didn't even try
to figure it out.

193
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,000
And when it looked like you had tried,

194
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,000
it was just fancy plating
with no flavor to back it up

195
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:15,000
It's clear that none of you
took this seriously.

196
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Yeah, but come on, pork? No matter how
you cook it, it's still just pork.

197
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:24,000
You wanna say that one more time?
If I hear any more crap from you,

198
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:28,000
I'll shove my arm up your ass,
and knock your teeth out! Got it?

199
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:30,000
[Buhara] Menchi’s temper is getting
the best of her again.

200
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,000
but I guess it's no surprise.

201
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,000
-There're only a few chefs in the world...
-...you wouldn't know gourmet cuisine...

202
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:37,000
-...who are good enough to satisfy her.
-You sorry excuse for a human.

203
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:39,000
I dare you to say it one more time!

204
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:42,000
So, as I was saying,
not a single one of you has the guts

205
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:45,000
to cook anything remotely new
or innovative.

206
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:47,000
Hey! Shut up!
I'm not here because I'm trying

207
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,000
to be some gourmet cook,
but a Hunter!

208
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,000
[crowd] That's right. You tell her!

209
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
[Todo]
My goal is to become a Blacklist Hunter,

210
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:58,000
and no stupid Gourmet Hunter
is gonna tell me I can't.

211
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:02,000
Then it's too bad that a stupid
Gourmet Hunter is your examiner.

212
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:05,000
Well, better luck next year, I guess.

213
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Huh? Why, you... Don't mess with me!

214
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:16,000
[Menchi] Buhara, please don't interfere.

215
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:21,000
I'm sorry, but it kinda looked like you
were gonna kill him if I didn't step in.

216
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,000
[chuckling] Probably.

217
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Let's get this straight.

218
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:30,000
We frequently venture into the dens
of ferocious beats,

219
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,000
in search of the finest ingredients.

220
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:37,000
And every Hunter is proficient
in at least some form of martial art.

221
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:40,000
You lack focus, and the will
to experiment with new things.

222
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:45,000
And that alone disqualifies you all
from becoming Hunters.

223
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:56,000
[Chairman] Well, that said,
it seems a bit excessive

224
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,000
to fail every single applicant.

225
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:04,000
[man]
The symbol of the Hunter's Association!

226
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,000
It must be someone
from the exam committee.

227
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,000
[crowd grunting]

228
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:12,000
[coughing and spluttering]

229
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,000
[man] Hey, wait. Who's the old man?

230
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:36,000
He is the Head of the Exam Committee,
and he's responsible for the Hunter Exam.

231
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,000
Chairman Netero.

232
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Oh, I just work behind the scenes.
It's not all that impressive.

233
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:47,000
I only intervene in the exams
when little issues like this one pop up.

234
00:15:48,000 --> 00:15:50,000
-Now, dear Menchi.
-Sir.

235
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:55,000
It's come to my attention that you've
chosen to fail all this year's applicants,

236
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:59,000
the reason being, as I understand it,
their general reluctance

237
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:02,000
-to challenge the unknown.
-[Menchi] No.

238
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:07,000
I'm sorry, sir, but I snapped
when a candidate insulted Gourmet Hunters.

239
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:11,000
And I'm afraid I made the exam
harder than necessary.

240
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:14,000
I see, but it seems you're aware

241
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:16,000
that this exam
was completely unacceptable.

242
00:16:16,000 --> 00:16:20,000
Yes. It's just that I get so emotional
when food is involved.

243
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,000
I'm not suited for this position.

244
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:27,000
So, I must resign as examiner.
Please let them retake the Second Phase.

245
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:32,000
Sadly, I can't imagine where we'd begin
to find an examiner on such short notice.

246
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:35,000
My deepest apologies, sir.

247
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
Hold on, I have an idea.

248
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
You continue serving as examiner,

249
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:44,000
but you yourself must participate
alongside this year's applicants,

250
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:46,000
in completing
whatever challenge you chose.

251
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:47,000
[gasps]

252
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
[Chairman]
Well, what do you say? Sound reasonable?

253
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:54,000
Surely that would make the applicants
more comfortable with the results.

254
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,000
I suppose you're right.

255
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:00,000
And I have just the thing
for the new challenge.

256
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
We'll all be making boiled eggs!

257
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:05,000
-[man] Boiled eggs?
-[indistinct chatter]

258
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:07,000
[Menchi] Chairman, since I see
you brought your airship,

259
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:10,000
would you mind taking us all
to Split Mountain?

260
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:15,000
[Chairman] Split Mountain?
Oh, I see. Yes, of course!

261
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:26,000
This is it.
Take a look at what's down there.

262
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:29,000
[man] What is that?

263
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:34,000
-A spider-eagle's web.
-They built their webs way down there?

264
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,000
[earth rumbling]

265
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:37,000
[gasps]

266
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Look past the web to what's underneath.

267
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:44,000
-[Killua] Hey, those are--
-[Menchi] Those are the spider-eagle eggs.

268
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:48,000
[Chairman] Spider-eagles build their webs
in deep ravines like this one.

269
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:51,000
It helps protect their eggs
from predators.

270
00:17:51,000 --> 00:17:56,000
That's what makes these eggs one of
the most difficult ingredients to obtain.

271
00:17:57,000 --> 00:18:00,000
Also, the eggs are commonly known
as "Dream Eggs."

272
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:04,000
-Hey, wait a minute. Do you mean--
-[Menchi] You bet I do.

273
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:05,000
Huh?

274
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
[all gasping]

275
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:19,000
[exhales]

276
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:24,000
Even if she grabs a few eggs,
how's she gonna climb back up?

277
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:29,000
[all gasp]

278
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:40,000
[Leorio] Hey! She jumped down!

279
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,000
Is she trying to get herself killed?

280
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:44,000
No, she's not.

281
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
[gasping]

282
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:56,000
That looks so fun.

283
00:18:56,000 --> 00:19:00,000
This ravine has updrafts
that are crucial to the spider-eagle.

284
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:03,000
Once they hatch, the wind currents
help guide their newborn chicks

285
00:19:03,000 --> 00:19:05,000
as they fly up to safety.

286
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:09,000
There! Now I just need to boil it
and I'll be set!

287
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:11,000
You gotta be kidding!

288
00:19:11,000 --> 00:19:15,000
You mean, you really expect us
to jump down there? That's crazy!

289
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:19,000
[Gon] I've been waiting
for something like this! [laughs]

290
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,000
[whooping]

291
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Alright, I'm in.

292
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Wait, I still haven't finished
explaining everything.

293
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,000
[man laughs] Later!

294
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:41,000
-What are we waiting for?
-Hold on! Don't let go yet.

295
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
-Why? What's wrong?
-No wind.

296
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:46,000
-The updrafts don't happen all the time.
-Huh?

297
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,000
[man screaming]

298
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,000
When do you think
the next one comes along?

299
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,000
Any minute now.

300
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Oh, crap! What the...?

301
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:06,000
It appears the web isn't strong enough
to support all this weight.

302
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,000
Gon, can we go yet?

303
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:14,000
Damn! I can't wait any longer.

304
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:19,000
[men screaming]

305
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:23,000
It's about to snap!

306
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Okay, now!

307
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:48,000
[chuckles]

308
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:52,000
What about you guys?
I'm guessing you quit?

309
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:55,000
[Chairman] Conceding takes courage, too.

310
00:21:03,000 --> 00:21:07,000
Unbelievable! This is way better
than what they sell in the store.

311
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:11,000
[munching]

312
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,000
I can see why
they're called Dream Eggs.

313
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:17,000
[Gon] Hey! Mr. Todo!

314
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:20,000
The egg's really good.
Do you wanna try it?

315
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:26,000
It's delicious.

316
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:28,000
[Menchi] The joy of discovering
something delicious.

317
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:31,000
And now, you know what it feels like.

318
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:34,000
That feeling is
what we risk our lives for.

319
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,000
I lost fair and square.

320
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,000
Next year, I'll be back.

321
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:46,000
[narrator] The applicants have learned
a valuable lesson.

322
00:21:46,000 --> 00:21:48,000
Whether Blacklist or Gourmet,

323
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:51,000
no one comes by
the title of Hunter easily.

324
00:21:51,000 --> 00:21:54,000
It requires a staggering amount
of determination.

325
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:59,000
Only 42 candidates remain.

326
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:03,000
[theme music plays]

327
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:28,000
[Gon] Next time,
"Showdown on the Airship."

328
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,000
Hey! Use soap when you wash your hands!

329
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:32,000
Right!
